15, and 2017. The final was a comfortable win for Yevloyev on points, 5-1."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The losing semi-finalists, who were seeded #3 and #4, were Poland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/146007"} "Tadeusz Michalik"] " and Iran’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/143834"} "Mohammadhadi Saravi"] ", but Yevloyev and Aleksanyan handled both of them easily. They went to the repêchage final, where they secured bronze medals, Michalik winning by technical superiority over Hungarian " [:a {:href "/athletes/143697"} "Alex Szőke"] " and Saravi defeating Finn " [:a {:href "/athletes/142688"} "Arvi Martin Savolainen"] " on points."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Classification Points", :class "footnote"} "CP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Victories by Fall", :class "footnote"} "VF"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Victories by Technical Superiority", :class "footnote"} "ST"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points", :class "footnote"} "TP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points Received", :class "footnote"} "TPR"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/146293"} "Musa Yevloyev"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ROC"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ROC.png"}] "ROC"]] [:td {} "12"] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "0"] [:td {} "21"] [:td {} "5"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/120952"} "Artur Aleksanyan"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ARM"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: 